The pinned map cannot load its own data. Here is the plan that loads the buildings upstream; then drop the map's "data" section so it draws the new node's output:

```json
{
  "goal": "Let the dashboard open: load the Loop buildings in a node of their own upstream of the pinned map.",
  "nodes": [
    {
      "ref": "loop-buildings",
      "nodeType": "curio.builtin/autk-grammar",
      "title": "Loop buildings",
      "intent": "Load the Chicago Loop's OpenStreetMap buildings with a spec that holds only the data section the Loop buildings map loads now: its osm load of docs/examples/data/chicago_loop.osm.pbf, its buildings layer, as table_osm."
    }
  ],
  "edges": [
    {
      "from": "loop-buildings",
      "to": "loop-map"
    }
  ]
}
```

Here is the plan that removes the chart; its tile leaves the dashboard with it:

```json
{
  "goal": "Delete the zip code bar chart.",
  "removeNodes": [
    "roofs-chart"
  ]
}
```
